Description:This figure displays the divergence between baseline and chaotic timelines over simulation time. The plot shows the state‑space distance (D(t)) increasing after perturbation injection, with distinct phases: stability window, chaotic lift‑off, full bifurcation, and attractor stabilization. The curve demonstrates how chaotic perturbations produce alternate futures while remaining physically plausible.

